From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shiny <owner@shinychang.net>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 17:05:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat: IDE-style browser shell on Chromium 156.0.8078.48

Single toolbar with no tab strip, avatar, app menu or bookmark bar; the
URL is centered and goes left-aligned while editing. Downloads is the
only pinned action, password saving and bookmark editing default off,
and the profile lives in "Chromium IDE".

New commands, registered as ActionItems because 156 routes browser
commands through the Actions framework:
- Cmd+T Go to Anything: open tabs by recency, history, recently closed,
  then open the URL or search in a new tab.
- Cmd+Shift+P command palette, not reserved so DevTools keeps its own.
- Ctrl+Tab cycles tabs in most-recently-used order with a hold overlay.
- Background tabs unfocused for 12 hours close automatically, except
  pinned, audible, capturing or unload-pending ones.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BYkQJUafT3hpFT1kBmDgzX
